the head of 10; a turn of 4 s at 100 frames a second from each sender; 16 groups of subcarriers;
the picture a disc 23 cm across in 5 mm pixels, 1654 of them; capacity 140 M MAC/s
  while turning, every report into the picture: 0.64 M/s = 0.5 %
  at the end of the turn, once:
    levelling the receivers (40 rounds): 81.9 M = 585 ms
    blurring the sums: 10.0 M = 71 ms
    the 3 x 3 solve in every pixel: 2.9 M = 20 ms
    carrying it back through the wall (FFT): 5.6 M = 40 ms
    together: 100 M = 0.72 s after the turn
  memory: the reduced reports of one turn 1.02 MB, the pixel sums 1.91 MB, against about 1.4 MB of RAM;
          the raw reports of one turn 5.1 MB go straight on to Kádrovák, not into RAM
